    "findings": [
      "The three selected item suppliers instantiate vanilla AxeItem in both archives. The selected ordinary EquipmentFeedback.damage route retains its prior code and the three template branches retain their return values, despite unrelated template branches changing.",
      "WeaponLift.groundSupport code is instruction-equivalent. The release adds longarm selection, and updates weapon, damage, tick, packet and accept code. Ground support here proves the sampled target-foot block contact shape, not a heavy-weapon strike contact.",
      "In the selected CombatFeedback comparison, only hit changes. The release drops the direct primaryLift >= .18 assignment of generic launch type 8 on this lane. The independently gated WeaponLift.tick owns an observed launch lane. The release EquipmentBehaviors changes are equipment/guard/counter paths and cannot substitute for a heavy impact receipt.",
      "Existing entity hit cues, trap/armor cues and combined visuals from a different weapon cannot establish paired contact-anchored shockwave and debris on these three registered weapons. No native attack was performed."
    ]
  },
